{"name":"Armadillo Egg","hex":"#7d4638","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"armadillo egg","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A jalapeño popper, especially when wrapped in bacon or sausage meat.","Used other than figuratively or idiomatically: see armadillo,‎ egg."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/armadillo_egg"}],"entries":[{"title":"Jalapeño popper","blocks":[{"text":"Jalapeño poppers, or jalapeño bites, are jalapeño peppers that have been hollowed out, stuffed with a mixture of cheese, spices, and sometimes ground meat, and breaded and deep-fried or wrapped with bacon and baked. They are a common dish on appetizer menus in chain restaurants in the United States."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Cooking-food-stuffed-jalapenos-peppers.jpg/330px-Cooking-food-stuffed-jalapenos-peppers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jalape%C3%B1o_popper"},{"title":"Armadillo","blocks":[{"text":"Armadillos are placental mammals in the order Cingulata. They form part of the superorder Xenarthra, along with the anteaters and sloths. Twenty-one extant species of armadillo have been described, some of which are distinguished by the number of bands on their armor. All species are native to the Americas, where they inhabit a variety of environments."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Nine-banded_Armadillo.jpg/330px-Nine-banded_Armadillo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Armadillo"},{"title":"Egg","blocks":[{"text":"An egg is an organic vessel grown by an animal to carry a possibly fertilized egg cell – a zygote. Within the vessel, an embryo is incubated until it has developed enough to survive on its own, at which point the animal hatches. Reproductive structures similar to the egg in other kingdoms are termed \"spores\", or in spermatophytes \"seeds\", or in gametophytes \"egg cells\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Adolphe_Millot_oeufs-fixed.jpg/330px-Adolphe_Millot_oeufs-fixed.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Egg"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Pink_Fairy_Armadillo_%28Chlamyphorus_truncatus%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Pink_Fairy_Armadillo_%28Chlamyphorus_truncatus%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Pink_Fairy_Armadillo_%28Chlamyphorus_truncatus%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Pink_Fairy_Armadillo_%28Chlamyphorus_truncatus%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APink_Fairy_Armadillo_(Chlamyphorus_truncatus)_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Nine-banded_armadillo_skeleton.jpg/500px-Nine-banded_armadillo_skeleton.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Nine-banded_armadillo_skeleton.jpg/1280px-Nine-banded_armadillo_skeleton.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Nine-banded_armadillo_skeleton.jpg/500px-Nine-banded_armadillo_skeleton.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Nine-banded armadillo skeleton","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANine-banded_armadillo_skeleton.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Three_Banded_Armadillo.jpg/500px-Three_Banded_Armadillo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/